  "subdivision": {
    "number": 2,
    "heading": "Assessment of Costs by Assessment Officer"
  },
  "operative_text": {
    "controlling": "10.43(1)  An assessment officer’s decision must be given by an\ninterim or final certificate, which may be endorsed on a bill of\ncosts, and which must\n(a) certify the amount to be paid by each party or person,\n(b) certify any special circumstance and the amount to be paid\nby each party or person with respect to the special\ncircumstance, and\n(c) be dated and signed by the assessment officer.\n(2)  A certificate that meets the requirements stated in subrule (1) is\nconclusive proof of the amount that a party or person who had\nnotice of the assessment must pay.",
    "controlling_carrier": "OFFICIAL",
    "sha256": "d930358b447a8c2d741e0addc1b6bf44f0a3954f19c01730d5bfbd53d9ca2155"
  },
